  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The overall superconducting characteristics of high-entropy alloys are primarily governed by effective valence electron count.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing uranium can suppress Tc by acting as a superconducting pair breaker.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Uranium introduces f-electron character into [TaNb]0.31(TiUHf)0.69.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Uranium-induced pair breaking arises from f-electron contributions and strong spin-orbit coupling.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "[TaNb]0.31(TiUHf)0.69 exhibits phonon-mediated superconductivity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Tc of [TaNb]0.31(TiUHf)0.69 is moderately suppressed relative to analogous Zr-containing alloys.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing U with Zr produces the proposed comparison alloy [TaNb]0.31(TiZrHf)0.69.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The U-containing alloy and its Zr analogue have body-centered-cubic structures.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Similar processing can maintain similar disorder levels in the U- and Zr-containing alloys.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-entropy alloys contain stochastic elemental distributions on simple crystalline lattices.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stochastic elemental distribution sets the effective valence electron count relevant to superconductivity.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Zr with U alters the local electronic environment through uranium's f electrons.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Effective valence electron count tunes electron-phonon coupling strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The uranium f electrons in this alloy are delocalized.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the same nominal valence electron count, the U-containing alloy will have a lower Tc than the Zr-containing control.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the same nominal valence electron count, the U-containing alloy will have a lower Hc2 than the Zr-containing control.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The U- and Zr-containing comparison alloys have the same nominal valence electron count.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of Tc and Hc2 suppression should correlate with the expected strength of uranium-induced pair breaking.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Zr-containing analogue follows a predictable Tc evolution based on valence electron count and has higher Tc and Hc2 than the U-containing alloy.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism is limited to phonon-mediated, weakly coupled HEAs in which disorder does not mask electron-phonon interactions and uranium is the only significant magnetic perturbation.",
